<body>

<div id="site">

<header class="bar">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="logo" href="#top">ACCO <span>Ahmed Construction Co.</span></a>
    <nav class="links">
      <a href="#estimator">Estimator</a>
      <a href="#plots">Plot sizes</a>
      <a href="#rates">Rates</a>
      <a href="#costs">Cost table</a>
      <a href="#payment">Payments</a>
      <a href="#brands">Materials</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>
    <a class="btn printhide" href="#contact">Get a quote</a>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ═══ HERO ═══ -->
<div class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="year-tag">EDITION 2026 · PAKISTAN</div>
    <h1>House construction cost, <em>priced per square foot.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">Gray structure and turnkey rates for residential construction across Pakistan — from a 5 Marla home to a 2 Kanal house. Use the estimator to price your own plot in seconds.</p>

    <div class="rates">
      <div class="rate">
        <div class="lbl">Gray structure</div>
        <div class="val">Rs 2,850<small>/ SFT</small></div>
        <div class="sub">Layout, excavation, foundation, RCC frame, masonry, plaster, staircase, water tanks.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rate">
        <div class="lbl">Standard finishing</div>
        <div class="val">Rs 2,800<small>/ SFT</small></div>
        <div class="sub">Tiles, marble, paint, doors, windows, POP ceiling, kitchen, wardrobes, MEP, boundary wall, MS gate and safety grills.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rate opt">
        <div class="lbl">Optional basement</div>
        <div class="val">Rs 5,500<small>/ SFT GRAY</small></div>
        <div class="val">Rs 2,800<small>/ SFT FINISHING</small></div>
        <div class="sub">Priced separately. Excavation, shoring, retaining walls and waterproofing drive the higher rate.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="citystrip">
      <b>Cities served</b>
      <span>Lahore · Islamabad · Rawalpindi · Karachi · Faisalabad · Multan · Gujranwala · Sialkot · Peshawar · and all major cities of Pakistan</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══ INTRODUCTION ═══ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">About this guide</p>
    <h2>What these rates cover, and what moves them</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">The figures in this guide are estimates for standard-quality residential construction in Pakistan during 2026. They are built on current market rates for material and labour and reflect the specification level most homeowners build to. Your final cost will sit above or below these numbers depending on the eight factors below — which is why every ACCO project starts with a measured BOQ rather than a per-square-foot guess.</p>

    <div class="grid3">
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 01</div><h4>City</h4><p>Material freight, labour availability and local levies differ between Lahore, Karachi, Islamabad and secondary cities.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 02</div><h4>Soil conditions</h4><p>Weak or waterlogged strata call for deeper footings, raft foundations or soil replacement.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 03</div><h4>Design complexity</h4><p>Long spans, cantilevers, double-height spaces and curved elements raise both steel and shuttering quantities.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 04</div><h4>Society bylaws</h4><p>DHA, Bahria Town and similar authorities set covered-area limits, elevation rules and approval fees.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 05</div><h4>Material selection</h4><p>The gap between standard and imported finishes is the single largest swing in a turnkey budget.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 06</div><h4>Labour rates</h4><p>Skilled trade rates move seasonally and with project density in the area.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 07</div><h4>Basement</h4><p>Excavation, shoring, retaining walls and waterproofing are priced separately from the standard rate.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 08</div><h4>Client specifications</h4><p>Home automation, lifts, solar systems, pools and bespoke joinery are additions to the base scope.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══ ESTIMATOR ═══ -->
<section class="tint" id="estimator">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Live estimator</p>
    <h2>Price your house</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Pick a plot size, adjust the covered area to your design, and choose your scope. The estimate updates instantly at the 2026 rates.</p>

    <div class="est">
      <div class="est-controls">
        <label class="ctrl-label" id="plotlabel">Plot size</label>
        <div class="chips" role="group" aria-labelledby="plotlabel" id="plotChips"></div>

        <div class="field">
          <label class="ctrl-label" for="area">Covered area (SFT)</label>
          <input type="number" id="area" min="200" max="60000" step="50" value="2000" inputmode="numeric">
          <div class="hint" id="areaHint">Standard double-storey covered area for this plot.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <span class="ctrl-label">Scope of work</span>
          <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Scope of work" id="scopeSeg">
            <button type="button" data-scope="gray">Gray structure</button>
            <button type="button" data-scope="finish">Finishing only</button>
            <button type="button" data-scope="turnkey" aria-pressed="true">Turnkey</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <span class="ctrl-label">Basement</span>
          <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Basement" id="bmtSeg">
            <button type="button" data-bmt="0" aria-pressed="true">No basement</button>
            <button type="button" data-bmt="1">Add basement</button>
          </div>
          <div id="bmtWrap" hidden style="margin-top:14px">
            <label class="ctrl-label" for="bmtArea">Basement area (SFT)</label>
            <input type="number" id="bmtArea" min="100" max="30000" step="50" value="1000" inputmode="numeric">
            <div class="hint">Defaults to the ground floor footprint. Basement is charged at Rs 5,500/SFT gray and Rs 2,800/SFT finishing.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <span class="ctrl-label">Quotation details <span style="text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;color:#8B9AAE">(optional)</span></span>
          <input type="text" id="qClient" placeholder="Client name" style="width:100%;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans';font-size:15px;padding:11px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:2px;margin-bottom:8px">
          <input type="text" id="qSite" placeholder="Plot no. / society / city" style="width:100%;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans';font-size:15px;padding:11px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:2px">
        </div>

        <div class="plotdraw">
          <span class="ctrl-label">Plot footprint</span>
          <svg id="plotSVG" viewBox="0 0 360 210" role="img" aria-labelledby="plotTitle"><title id="plotTitle">Plot dimension drawing</title></svg>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="est-out" id="estOut">
        <div class="out-row">
          <div class="k">Gray structure<em>@ RS 2,850 / SFT</em></div>
          <div class="v" id="oGray">—</div>
        </div>
        <div class="out-row">
          <div class="k">Standard finishing<em>@ RS 2,800 / SFT</em></div>
          <div class="v" id="oFin">—</div>
        </div>
        <div class="out-row" id="rowBmtG" hidden>
          <div class="k">Basement — gray<em>@ RS 5,500 / SFT</em></div>
          <div class="v" id="oBmtG">—</div>
        </div>
        <div class="out-row" id="rowBmtF" hidden>
          <div class="k">Basement — finishing<em>@ RS 2,800 / SFT</em></div>
          <div class="v" id="oBmtF">—</div>
        </div>
        <div class="out-row">
          <div class="k">Covered area<em>PRICED QUANTITY</em></div>
          <div class="v" id="oArea">—</div>
        </div>

        <div class="out-row">
          <div class="k">Completion time<em id="oDurBreak">GRAY + FINISHING</em></div>
          <div class="v" id="oDur">—</div>
        </div>

        <div class="split" aria-hidden="true"><i class="g" id="barG" style="width:50%"></i><i class="f" id="barF" style="width:50%"></i></div>
        <div class="legend"><span><s class="g" style="background:#5FA3E8"></s>Gray</span><span><s class="f" style="background:#0057B8"></s>Finishing</span></div>

        <div class="total">
          <div class="k" id="totalLabel">Total construction cost</div>
          <div class="big" id="oTotal">—</div>
          <div class="alt" id="oAlt">—</div>
        </div>

        <button class="btn" type="button" id="qGen" style="width:100%;margin-top:20px;padding:14px;font-size:15px">Create PDF quotation</button>
        <p class="disclaim">Estimate only. Excludes land, approval fees, utility connections and any client-specified additions such as lifts, solar, pools or home automation. Basement pricing is subject to a soil investigation report. ACCO issues a line-item BOQ before any contract is signed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══ PLOT SIZES ═══ -->
<section id="plots">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Reference data</p>
    <h2>Standard residential plot sizes</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Dimensions used across DHA, Bahria Town, LDA, CDA and private housing societies. Covered area shown is a typical double-storey build within normal bylaw coverage.</p>

    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Plot size</th>
            <th>Standard dimensions</th>
            <th class="num">Plot area (SFT)</th>
            <th>Corner plot (approx.)</th>
            <th class="num">Covered area, double storey</th>
            <th class="num">Completion time</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="name">5 Marla</td><td class="mono">25' × 45'</td><td class="num">1,125</td><td class="mono">30' × 45'</td><td class="num">2,000 SFT</td><td class="num">120 days<br><span style="color:#5A6B82;font-size:12px">≈ 4 months</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="name">7 Marla</td><td class="mono">30' × 52'</td><td class="num">1,575</td><td class="mono">35' × 52'</td><td class="num">2,800 SFT</td><td class="num">150 days<br><span style="color:#5A6B82;font-size:12px">≈ 5 months</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="name">8 Marla</td><td class="mono">30' × 60'</td><td class="num">1,800</td><td class="mono">35' × 60'</td><td class="num">3,000 SFT</td><td class="num">165 days<br><span style="color:#5A6B82;font-size:12px">≈ 5.5 months</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="name">10 Marla</td><td class="mono">35' × 65'</td><td class="num">2,275</td><td class="mono">40' × 65'</td><td class="num">3,450 SFT</td><td class="num">180 days<br><span style="color:#5A6B82;font-size:12px">≈ 6 months</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="name">1 Kanal</td><td class="mono">50' × 90'</td><td class="num">4,500</td><td class="mono">55' × 90'</td><td class="num">5,500 SFT</td><td class="num">210 days<br><span style="color:#5A6B82;font-size:12px">≈ 7 months</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="name">2 Kanal</td><td class="mono">75' × 120'</td><td class="num">9,000</td><td class="mono">80' × 120'</td><td class="num">11,000 SFT</td><td class="num">270 days<br><span style="color:#5A6B82;font-size:12px">≈ 9 months</span></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="tbl-note">Completion time is gray structure plus finishing, running from mobilisation to handover, on a 60:40 split between the two. A 10 Marla house completes in 6 months. A basement adds 60 days to any house. Corner plots carry extra frontage and boundary wall length, which adds to the finishing quantity even when covered area stays the same.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══ RATES / SCOPE ═══ -->
<section class="tint" id="rates">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">2026 rates</p>
    <h2>What is included in each rate</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Two rates, one specification standard. Combine both for a turnkey house handed over ready to occupy.</p>

    <div class="two">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Gray structure</h3>
        <div class="price">Rs 2,850<small>PER SQUARE FOOT</small></div>
        <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:0">The complete structural shell — everything up to a plastered, roofed, watertight building.</p>
        <ul class="check">
          <li>Site layout</li><li>Excavation</li><li>Foundation</li><li>PCC</li>
          <li>RCC frame structure</li><li>Columns</li><li>Beams</li><li>Roof slab</li>
          <li>Brick masonry</li><li>Cement plaster</li><li>Staircase</li>
          <li>Underground water tank</li><li>Overhead water tank</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Standard finishing</h3>
        <div class="price">Rs 2,800<small>PER SQUARE FOOT</small></div>
        <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:0">Everything that turns the shell into a finished, serviced, move-in home.</p>
        <ul class="check">
          <li>Floor tiles</li><li>Marble</li><li>Wall tiles</li><li>Paint</li>
          <li>Doors</li><li>Windows</li><li>False ceiling / POP</li><li>Kitchen</li>
          <li>Wardrobes</li><li>Electrical works</li><li>Plumbing works</li>
          <li>Sanitary fixtures</li><li>Glass works</li><li>Boundary wall</li>
          <li>Main gate — MS, 16 gauge</li><li>MS door frames — 16 gauge</li>
          <li>Safety grills</li><li>Driveway</li><li>Landscaping</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="tbl-note"><b>Combined turnkey rate: <span class="mono">Rs 5,650 per square foot</span> of covered area.</b><br>
    Basis of measurement — all quantities are measured on covered area only, as shown on the approved drawings. Boundary wall, main gate and driveway are included in the finishing rate and are not measured separately.</p>

    <div class="card" style="margin-top:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--blue-bright)">
      <h3>Optional basement — priced separately</h3>
      <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);max-width:70ch;margin:0 0 18px">A basement is not part of the standard per-square-foot rate. Excavation depth, shoring, retaining walls, structural waterproofing, dewatering, ramp and forced ventilation all sit outside the above-ground scope, which is why the rate is higher. Basement area is charged on its own.</p>
