<!-- ═══ TIMELINE ═══ -->
<section class="dark" id="timeline">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Programme</p>
    <h2>How the build runs, stage by stage</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">The payment schedule follows the physical sequence of work. Each stage is inspected and signed off before the next begins, and before the instalment against it is invoiced.</p>

    <ol class="timeline">
      <li>
        <div class="tl-pct">20%</div>
        <div class="tl-body">
          <h4>Mobilisation</h4>
          <p>Contract signing, site handover, drawings issued for construction, labour hutting, water and power connection, first material procurement, layout marking.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="tl-pct">15%</div>
        <div class="tl-body">
          <h4>Substructure to plinth</h4>
          <p>Excavation, PCC, foundation and footings, column starter bars, plinth beam, back-filling and compaction, damp proof course. Basement raft and retaining walls sit here where a basement is included.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="tl-pct">20%</div>
        <div class="tl-body">
          <h4>Ground floor walls</h4>
          <p>Ground floor columns cast to slab soffit, 9" and 4.5" brick masonry, door and window frames set, conduiting laid in walls.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="tl-pct">20%</div>
        <div class="tl-body">
          <h4>Ground floor slab</h4>
          <p>Shuttering, slab reinforcement, electrical conduits in slab, concrete pour, curing, staircase flight to first floor.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="tl-pct">20%</div>
        <div class="tl-body">
          <h4>First floor walls and slab</h4>
          <p>First floor columns, masonry, roof slab cast, mumty and parapet, overhead tank, internal and external cement plaster.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="tl-pct">5%</div>
        <div class="tl-body">
          <h4>Completion and handover</h4>
          <p>Finishing trades closed out, testing and commissioning of electrical and plumbing, cleaning, snag list cleared, keys and as-built drawings handed over.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <h3 style="margin-top:44px;font-size:20px">Completion time by plot size</h3>
    <p class="section-lede" style="font-size:15px">Calendar days from mobilisation to handover, split 60:40 between gray structure and finishing. A 10 Marla house completes in 6 months. A basement adds 60 days to any house.</p>
